// Title: RunDLL32 Spawning Explorer
// Sigma ID: caa06de8-fdef-4c91-826a-7f9e163eef4b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: elhoim, CD_ROM_
// Date: 2022-04-27 | Modified: 2022-05-25
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218.011
// Description: Detects RunDLL32.exe spawning explorer.exe as child, which is very uncommon, often observes
//   Gamarue spawning the explorer.exe process in an unusual way
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/intelligence-insights-november-2021/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_spawn_explorer.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe") and (not(InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "\\shell32.dll,Control_RunDLL"))
